# PLACEHOLDER — replace the contents of this file with the PUBLIC half of the
# deploy keypair used by .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Generate a dedicated keypair (do NOT reuse a personal key):
#
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "github-actions-deploy@klaus" -f deploy_key -N ""
#
# Then:
#   * put the contents of deploy_key.pub into THIS file (replacing these lines)
#   * store the contents of deploy_key (the private key) in the GitHub repo
#     secret named DEPLOY_SSH_KEY
#   * delete the local deploy_key / deploy_key.pub afterwards
#
# sshd ignores blank lines and lines beginning with '#', so until you replace
# this file no CI key is trusted by root — the config still evaluates and
# builds fine. Bootstrap the first switch over the LAN/VPN with
# `just deploy klaus` so root picks up the real key before deploying from CI.
